  "chosen_rule": {
    "rule_id": "P19-M1",
    "name": "keep-all + observation mask channel",
    "statement": "No timestep and no sample is dropped or imputed. Every window keeps all L timesteps. A timestep whose calendar day is absent from the model table is written to the tensor as all-NaN in Dataset B and handed to the model as mask=0 (binary mask channel, sequence_mask_L{L}.npy); observed days are mask=1. On present days the ~0.1% variable-level NaNs (precip_mm, tmax_c, tmin_c) are replaced by 0 AFTER the training fold's standardisation, i.e. by the fold mean - no information, no fitting outside the fold. Phase 21 input is therefore concat(12 raw variables, mask) = 13 channels; a plain NaN must never reach a layer.",
    "why": [
      "identical sample sets for L = 3/7/14/30 - the D12 length sweep stays comparable (rejection would train different models on different data)",
      "nothing is fabricated: interpolation/forward-fill would invent driver variables (precip_mm), age-2 filling (R4) still drops samples",
      "the cheapest rejected alternative (R2) drops 2.9-26.7% of samples, L-dependent and distribution-shifting (S3b)"
    ],
    "samples_dropped_per_L": {
      "3": 0,
      "7": 0,
      "14": 0,
      "30": 0
    }
  },
